Q: How do I have to configure Visual Studio Code, so I don&#39;t get a &quot;undefined reference&quot; error message? A: <p>You need to edit the <em><a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/debugtest/tasks" rel="nofollow noreferrer">tasks.json</a></em> file, generated by Visual Studio Code.</p>
<p>When you debug a simple <em>.cpp</em> file with a <em>main</em> function, the default configuration of <em>tasks.json</em> is enough, but if you try to use a personal headers files with classes, you need to indicate to <em>tasks.json</em> which extra files your program need in order to compile.</p>
<p>Like this:</p>
<pre><code>  {
    &quot;tasks&quot;: [
        {
            &quot;type&quot;: &quot;shell&quot;,
            &quot;label&quot;: &quot;g++ build active file&quot;,
            &quot;command&quot;: &quot;/usr/bin/g++&quot;,
            &quot;args&quot;: [
                &quot;-g&quot;,
                &quot;${file}&quot;,&quot;${fileDirname}/Node.cpp&quot;, &lt;============= HERE &lt;======
                &quot;-o&quot;,
                &quot;${fileDirname}/${fileBasenameNoExtension}&quot;
            ],
            &quot;options&quot;: {
                &quot;cwd&quot;: &quot;/usr/bin&quot;
            }
        }
    ],
    &quot;version&quot;: &quot;2.0.0&quot;
}
</code></pre>
<p>In the section <strong>args</strong>, I just added the full path of my extra <em>.cpp</em> file (<em>ej.&quot;${fileDirname}/extrefile.cpp&quot;</em>).</p>
<p>Save the <em>tasks.json</em> file and run the Debugging again with <kbd>F5</kbd>, from the *<em>.cpp</em> file with the <em>main</em> function.</p>

Q: Mocking EF DbContext with Moq A: <p>You can use <a href="https://github.com/ramantsitou/MockQueryable" rel="nofollow noreferrer">MockQueryable</a>. Here is the example:</p>
<pre><code>var users = new List&lt;UserEntity&gt;
{
    new UserEntity { LastName = &quot;Smith&quot;, DateOfBirth = new DateTime(2012, 1, 20) },
    // More test data...
};

var mockDbSet = users.BuildMockDbSet();

await mockDbSet.AnyAsync(x =&gt; ...);
await mockDbSet.FirstOrDefaultAsync(x =&gt; ...);
await mockDbSet.ToListAsync();
// etc.
</code></pre>
<p>It supports Moq, NSubstitute and FakeItEasy</p>
